 "title": "A record and what belongs to it: an invoice",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail stands shut to its icons, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The page level is the record, an invoice the platform sent to an organization: the way back, its number, and on the line under the number its state, the organization it was sent to and its total. A state that is not the normal one is a badge, and it stands before the other facts: the end of the page level holds actions only. Then the lists attached to the record, each a container: the lines the invoice is made of, the payments tried against it, and the emails sent about it. Each is only read, so none has a box at its top that finds a record to add. The lists stand side by side at a desktop, and one under another on a tablet and a phone. Every screen shows every list. No list shows a count.",
